ltrace FTBFS on alpha with the following error:

gcc -Wall -g -O2 -iquote /=ABPKGBUILDDIR=BB -iquote
/=ABPKGBUILDDIR=BB/sysdeps/linux-gnu -DSYSCONFDIR=3D\"/etc\"  -I
/usr/include/libelf -I/=ABPKGBUILDDIR=BB/sysdeps/linux-gnu/alpha  -c -o
trace.o trace.c
In file included from trace.c:10:0:
/=ABPKGBUILDDIR=BB/debug.h:6:2: error: redeclaration of enumerator 'DEBUG=
_EVENT'
/=ABPKGBUILDDIR=BB/debug.h:6:2: note: previous definition of 'DEBUG_EVENT=
'
was here

Full build log at:
http://buildd.debian-ports.org/status/fetch.php?pkg=3Dltrace&arch=3Dalpha=
&ver=3D0.5.3-2.1&stamp=3D1333340950

The error arises because the include file "debug.h" gets included twice
by sysdeps/linux-gnu/alpha/trace.c leading to the above quoted error.

Patch fixing the problem attached.

Cheers
Michael.



--------------060107030604030507020702
Content-Type: text/x-patch;
 name="alpha-dont-include-already-include-debug-h.patch"
Content-Disposition: attachment;
 filename="alpha-dont-include-already-include-debug-h.patch"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 7bit

--- ltrace-0.5.3/sysdeps/linux-gnu/alpha/trace.c	2009-07-26 03:13:02.000000000 +1200
+++ ltrace-0.5.3-new/sysdeps/linux-gnu/alpha/trace.c	2012-06-24 13:05:28.000000000 +1200
@@ -7,7 +7,6 @@
 #include <asm/ptrace.h>
 
 #include "common.h"
-#include "debug.h"
 
 #if (!defined(PTRACE_PEEKUSER) && defined(PTRACE_PEEKUSR))
 # define PTRACE_PEEKUSER PTRACE_PEEKUSR

--------------060107030604030507020702--





